+      "external": false,
+      "kind": "GAP",
+      "evidence": "Section 1 requires retaining resources needed by 'surviving or unverified owned processes.' Section 2 requires resume to reconcile persisted facts 'with Git and tracker state before admitting affected work,' while fresh admission checks holds, cancellation and dependencies. Task super-plan-ufz.12 likewise defines reconciliation against Git/tracker and tests valid landings, holds and mismatches. None specifies how a surviving or unverified unfinished attempt constrains resumed admission. Consider interruption before landing, with the previous attempt still using its retained workspace: Git/tracker can correctly show unfinished work without establishing that restarting it is safe. Resource retention alone does not settle whether resume must wait, reconnect, verify termination, or isolate a replacement attempt and exclude the old attempt's eventual result. That cross-boundary decision is necessary to preserve work through the explicitly supported survivor/unknown outcome."
